      "writtenOn": "2023-06-30T06:48:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is eminently dangerous because the constructor is not running on the thread where you use this var. Only `final` gives you the guarantee that this initialization is seen.\n\nIn this case it will work only because false is the default value of boolean. In fact, this should probably be called `mEnabled` rather than `mDisabled` because positive meanings are easier to understand than negative ones (you have to do some mental gymnastics to understand \"not disabled\"). But if you make this true, it won\u0027t work.\n\nIf that\u0027s where you\u0027re going to leave it, I\u0027d tell you to write a detailed comment about this. Unfortunately, https://android-review.git.corp.google.com/c/platform/packages/modules/Connectivity/+/2646399/2/service/src/com/android/server/connectivity/KeepaliveStatsTracker.java#287 sets this to true in the constructor, and it will be seen as false on the handler thread some of the time, so you\u0027ll still bootloop the system. Thus you must find a solution to this.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 84,
        "startChar": 32,
        "endLine": 84,
        "endChar": 37
      },
      "revId": "515e2345fc4b67f1f44c730ab2689b18b70bbc82",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
